Generate the wit-dylib adapters with the stack pointer in task context slot 0.

SDK 34's wasm32-wasip3 libc, and the runtime built against it, keep the
stack pointer in task context slot 0, which libc's task hooks set for each
task (the main stack, or one of its own). wit-dylib's adapters (the
trampolines around every import and export) default to an imported
`__stack_pointer` global, which nothing moves: their frames start at the top
of the main stack whatever the task runs on, over the runtime's outermost
frames. A sync import with its parameters in memory (Pane's
`feedback.show-toast`) called after an async export resumed overwrote the
runtime's QuickJS context there, and the callback crashed. wit-dylib 0.258's
`StackPointer::TaskContext` is the WASIp3 ABI.

Modifies componentize-qjs (Apache-2.0, see LICENSE-componentize-qjs); this
patch is distributed under the same license.

--- a/crates/core/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/core/src/lib.rs
@@ -125,7 +125,16 @@ pub async fn componentize(opts: &ComponentizeOpts<'_>) -> Result<Vec<u8>> {
     let world_id = resolve.select_world(&[pkg_id], opts.world_name)?;
 
     let resolver = module_resolution(opts)?;
-    let (mut wit_dylib, wit_metadata) = wit_dylib::create_with_metadata(&resolve, world_id, None);
+    // The runtime and SDK 34's P3 libc keep the stack pointer in task
+    // context slot 0, so the generated adapters must too: with the default
+    // (an imported `__stack_pointer` global, which nothing else moves) their
+    // frames start at the top of the main stack, over the runtime's own.
+    let mut dylib_opts = wit_dylib::DylibOpts {
+        stack_pointer: wit_dylib::StackPointer::TaskContext,
+        ..Default::default()
+    };
+    let (mut wit_dylib, wit_metadata) =
+        wit_dylib::create_with_metadata(&resolve, world_id, Some(&mut dylib_opts));
     let shim = codegen::generate_shim(&resolve, &wit_metadata);
 
